# Cursor context improvement

- Update repository/module profiles when tracked manifests, commands, contracts, or ownership
  change; do not add aspirations unsupported by code or CI.
- Keep only two root always-applied rules. Scope technology rules and keep procedures in skills.
- Never add credentials, remote executable context, duplicate MCP authority, or module hooks.
- Preserve globally unique module-qualified skill names and validate module index digests.
- Run both Cursor validators after context changes and report any discovery check that requires
  manual Cursor UI verification.
